course: dictionary
lesson: 3412
title: Export: sending goods abroad
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Export can work as a verb or a noun, so read the sentence to see which job it does. As a verb, to export means to send goods to another country to sell them. «Much Ming porcelain was exported in huge numbers» means many pieces were sent to other countries to be sold.
explain: As a noun, an export is the thing that is sold abroad. «Exports are goods a country sells abroad and imports are goods it buys from abroad.» Here exports means the goods themselves.
explain: Look for the opposite to find the meaning. Import is the opposite of export, so the sentence tells you that export means selling abroad and import means buying from abroad. Swap your meaning into the sentence: «A country sells goods abroad» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Export means to send goods to another country to sell them.
fact: An export is something sold to another country, and the plural is exports.
fact: Import is the opposite of export: an import is something bought from abroad.
fact: Countries export what they grow or make: New Zealand exports lamb and butter, and Australia exports iron ore.
fact: In computing, to export means to save data in a form another program can use, as in «export as PDF».
exercise: What is an export? | A country's flag | *Something sold to another country | Something bought from another country | A rule for trading
exercise: Which word is the opposite of export? | *Import | Porcelain | Abroad | Trade
exercise: «Much Ming porcelain was exported in huge numbers.» What does exported mean here? | Hidden away in a museum | *Sent to other countries to be sold | Painted blue | Broken into small pieces
test: New Zealand exports lamb and butter. Which is true? | New Zealand buys lamb and butter from abroad | Lamb and butter are a kind of money | Lamb and butter are kept only for New Zealand families | *New Zealand sends lamb and butter abroad to be sold
test: Click File, then export as PDF. What does export mean here? | Hide the file in a folder | Print the file on paper | Delete the file | *Save the file in a form another program can use
exam: «Exports are goods a country sells abroad and imports are goods it buys from abroad.» Which is an import? | Something made at home and kept there | Goods a country sells abroad | The business of selling goods abroad | *Goods a country buys from abroad
